ORIGINAL THEORETICAL CONTRIBUTIONS — INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY NOTICE

The following theoretical constructs are original intellectual contributions of
Ciprian Stefan Plesca and are protected as such:

  • Entropic Threat Continuum (ETC) — including all formal axioms, definitions,
    and the five-tuple formalization (S, A, T, D, E)
  • Adversarial Entropy Gradient (AEG) — including the formal definition
    G(s,a) = dH(s)/dE(a) and all associated thermodynamic analysis
  • Trust Decay Function (TDF) — including the formal model
    T(c,t) = T(c,0) · exp(−λ(c)·t) · f(B(c,t))
  • Dark Topology Conjecture (DTC) — including the graph-theoretic conjecture
    relating algebraic connectivity to k-anonymity bounds
  • Layered Anonymity Stack (LAS) — the six-layer formal protocol-stack model
  • Threat Surface Integral (TSI) — the line integral formulation of
    organizational exposure
  • Contextual Exposure Principle (CEP) — and its formal proof in Appendix A
  • Opacity Migration Theorem (OMT) — and its formal statement
  • Plesca Taxonomy — the three-axis, four-level attack classification system
    comprising 847 discrete attack primitive types
  • Three-Tier Stratification of Dark Network Infrastructure

Any academic work that builds upon, extends, critiques, or applies these
constructs must provide full attribution to this dissertation.

